From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(DisksMenu): only RetroForge's partitions and the SD card
 are shown

The Disks settings menu listed every partition of every drive udisks2
did not consider protected: on a handheld that is ~85 vendor partitions
of the internal storage, while RetroForge's own partitions, on the same
drive as /, were never shown. It now shows only the partitions mounted
at /, /var, /efi, /esp and /home, and the SD card at
/run/retroforge/sdcard, each when mounted. The device behind each mount
point is read from /proc/self/mountinfo and sysfs (for btrfs, whose
device number is anonymous, from the mount's source, following a /dev
symlink), and each drive's card lists only those partitions. "No storage
mounted" shows when none is. UDisks2Instance signals devices added and
removed but not mounts and unmounts, so the cards are rebuilt each time
the menu is shown.

Sizes are shown as df shows them: a partition card the mounted
filesystem's size and free space in binary units, from df, and a drive
card the drive's size in binary units from sysfs. udisks2's readable
size is the partition's in decimal units: a 256 MiB /var showed as
"268.44 MB" where df shows "224M".
